      },
      "question": {
        ":question/problem": "Find the product $AB$, if\n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}3\\sqrt{10} & -1 & 4.6 \\\\ -4 & 2\\sqrt{11} & -1.7 \\\\ 3\\sqrt{6} & 6 & 9\\end{bmatrix}$\nand \n$B=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that $B$ is the $3$rd *column* of the identity matrix ${I}_{3}.$\n\nSince we're multiplying the $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$ by the $3$rd *column* of the identity matrix ${I}_{3},$ the result must be the $3$rd *column* of $A.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nAB=\\begin{bmatrix}4.6 \\\\ -1.7 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nLet's check the long way:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\begin{bmatrix}3\\sqrt{10} & -1 & 4.6 \\\\ -4 & 2\\sqrt{11} & -1.7 \\\\ 3\\sqrt{6} & 6 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3\\sqrt{10}\\cdot 0+(-1)\\cdot 0+4.6\\cdot 1 \\\\ (-4)\\cdot 0+2\\sqrt{11}\\cdot 0+(-1.7)\\cdot 1 \\\\ 3\\sqrt{6}\\cdot 0+6\\cdot 0+9\\cdot 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4.6 \\\\ -1.7 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
