      "question": {
        ":question/problem": "Find the product $AB,$ if\n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}2\\sqrt{13} & -3 & 6 \\\\ 3 & \\sqrt{3} & -1 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$\nand \n$B=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $AB=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  |\n|  |  | {{field-3}} |  |",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that $B$ is the $2$nd *column* of the identity matrix ${I}_{3}.$\n\nSince we're multiplying the $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$ by the $2$nd *column* of the identity matrix ${I}_{3},$ the result must be the $2$nd *column* of $A.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nAB=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nLet's check the long way:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\begin{bmatrix}2\\sqrt{13} & -3 & 6 \\\\ 3 & \\sqrt{3} & -1 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2\\sqrt{13}\\cdot 0+(-3)\\cdot 1+6\\cdot 0 \\\\ 3\\cdot 0+\\sqrt{3}\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot 0 \\\\ 7\\cdot 0+(-1)\\cdot 1+0\\cdot 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
